{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/215804-the-ancient-sumer-angle-in-idigam-chronicles","id":215804,"title":"The Ancient Sumer angle in Idigam Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-01T06:31:30-07:00","id":215804,"title":"The Ancient Sumer angle in Idigam Chronicles","content":"Much like Mage's Atlantis myth is getting shuffled to the end of its Chronicle book, I was wondering how the proto-Sumer stuff in Werewolf might be treated in The Idigam Chronicle. Alternatively, how's it been covered presently? I get that it's one of the less important details of Werewolf's mythos, the important bits being Luna, Mother Wolf, and the Spirit-Flesh divide, but as a fan of history I find it interesting.<br /> <br /> As an alternate question, how much Sumerian influence do you <i>want</i> to see in Idigam Chronicle? I don't need much myself, and am fine if it gets completely cut to save some word count. Werewolf doesn't seem like a game that would benefit from having a strong historical influence on the characters. Plus metaplot, megaplot, inflexible backstory, etc...Obviously want to avoid that.<br /> <br /> The IC game I'm planning won't involve any of that stuff. It's gonna be all about the Forsaken versus the Pure and lead into cleaning up the spiritual fallout in the pack's new territory. But what about y'all? How have you worked in Ancient Sumer and the werewolves' history as Feral God-Kings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:31:26-07:00","id":215836,"title":"","content":"I don't expect to see much. It's not like it was overly present in Forsaken. Just First Tongue (which I'd keep the same) and a shard/Hunting Grounds in the Chronicler's Guide.<br /> <br /> To be perfectly honest, I wouldn't mind a little more but <i>it's not needed</i>. Particularly since they seem to be going to a lot of effort to help you localize the Chronicles to fit your group's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:00:03-07:00","id":215861,"title":"","content":"I know it's not needed. As I mentioned, I'm not planning on incorporating it at all in my upcoming game. I just think it's one interesting thing to talk about regarding the backstory that doesn't get as much coverage as everything else. Also, my other favorite game in WoD is Mummy, so the ancient, proto-Sumer angle makes it a more viable candidate for crossovers. Guess I'm just a little biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:18:36-07:00","id":216109,"title":"","content":"The Forsaken Storyteller's Guide has a bit on playing in Ancient Sumer that I thought was pretty neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:45:20-07:00","id":216128,"title":"","content":"I'd, personally, like more; however, it's not really needed. In my personal Chronicle it was a time and place where the Forsaken where strong, and where Spirits left an indelible mark on humans, but nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br